3	//! Boot-time reconciliation of the starter Cedar policy set + the seven system roles
4	//! (SMA-444 Task 17, design §3.2/D6/M5). [`reconcile_starter`] runs once per `AppState::new`
5	//! (the composition root), AFTER the policy store is constructed but BEFORE the initial
6	//! `PolicySnapshot` compiles — so a fresh/unseeded database gets the starter policies (and
7	//! role catalog) seeded before the first request is ever decided, and every process restart
8	//! is idempotent: an unchanged starter policy is a no-op, a changed one is a WARN (never a
9	//! silent overwrite — the store itself refuses to edit a persisted `system = true` row, so
10	//! attempting one would error, not drift), and an already-present role row is left alone.
11	//! This is boot code, so it touches the `role` SeaORM entity directly rather than going
12	//! through a port — there is no `RoleRepository` port (roles are code-defined; this table is
13	//! only their persisted/introspectable form and the `role_grant.role_key` FK target).
14	
